diff --git a/PACKAGING.md b/PACKAGING.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2beb710
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PACKAGING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,129 @@
+# Packaging OpenLiteSpeed for Linux Distributions
+
+This document describes the CMake build options added to support building
+OpenLiteSpeed against system shared libraries and installing to
+FHS-compliant paths.  These changes allow the project to be packaged by
+Linux distributions that require shared-library linking and standard
+directory layouts.
+
+## New CMake Options
+
+### `USE_SYSTEM_LIBS` (default: `OFF`)
+
+When set to `ON`, the build uses `find_package()` and `pkg_check_modules()`
+to locate system-installed versions of every library that OpenLiteSpeed
+normally bundles as a static archive:
+
+| Library | How it is found | Upstream bundled form |
+|---|---|---|
+| OpenSSL | `find_package(OpenSSL)` | BoringSSL static (`libssl.a`, `libcrypto.a`, `libdecrepit.a`) |
+| zlib | `find_package(ZLIB)` | `libz.a` |
+| PCRE | `pkg_check_modules(PCRE libpcre)` | `libpcre.a` |
+| Expat | `find_package(EXPAT)` | `libexpat.a` |
+| libxml2 | `find_package(LibXml2)` | `libxml2.a` |
+| Brotli | `pkg_check_modules(BROTLI libbrotlienc libbrotlidec)` | `libbrotli*-static.a` |
+| libmaxminddb | `pkg_check_modules(MAXMINDDB libmaxminddb)` | `libmaxminddb.a` |
+| udns | `find_library(udns)` | `libudns.a` |
+| IP2Location | `find_library(IP2Location)` | `libIP2Location.a` |
+
+When `USE_SYSTEM_LIBS=ON`:
+
+* The build does **not** add `-DHAVE_BORINGSSL`.  BoringSSL-specific code
+  paths are skipped; standard OpenSSL API is used instead.  The code
+  already uses `<openssl/ssl.h>` style includes which work with both.
+* The `-D_GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI=0` hack (needed for the bundled static
+  `libstdc++.a`) is removed, allowing normal C++ ABI.
+* The `-nodefaultlibs` flag and manual listing of `libstdc++.a gcc_eh c
+  c_nonshared gcc` are replaced with normal dynamic linking.
+* Brotli and MaxMindDB are **optional** — if not found, the build
+  continues with those features disabled and a warning is printed.
+
+### `FHS_LAYOUT` (default: `OFF`)
+
+When set to `ON`, the build installs files to Filesystem Hierarchy
+Standard paths rather than the traditional `/usr/local/lsws` monolithic
+tree.
+
+#### Path mapping
+
+| Content | FHS path (with `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr`) |
+|---|---|
+| Server binary | `/usr/sbin/openlitespeed` |
+| Control script | `/usr/sbin/lswsctrl` |
+| Configuration | `/etc/openlitespeed/` |
+| Log files | `/var/log/openlitespeed/` |
+| Runtime / PID | `/var/run/openlitespeed/` |
+| Modules (`.so`) | `/usr/lib64/openlitespeed/modules/` |
+| Shared data | `/usr/share/openlitespeed/` |
+| Admin web UI | `/usr/share/openlitespeed/admin/` |
+| Default docroot | `/srv/openlitespeed/` |
+| Temp / swap | `/var/run/openlitespeed/tmp/` |
+
+All paths are configurable via `OLS_CONF_DIR`, `OLS_LOG_DIR`,
+`OLS_RUN_DIR`, `OLS_LIB_DIR`, `OLS_SHARE_DIR`, `OLS_DOC_ROOT`, and
+`OLS_TMP_DIR` CMake cache variables.
+
+When `FHS_LAYOUT=ON`, the C code receives compile-time defines
+(`FHS_CONF_DIR`, `FHS_LOG_DIR`, etc.) so that the server discovers its
+configuration from the fixed system path rather than probing relative to
+the binary location.
+
+## Quick Start — Building with system libraries
+
+```sh
+# Install build dependencies (Fedora / OpenMandriva example)
+sudo dnf install cmake ninja-build gcc g++ \
+    openssl-devel zlib-devel pcre-devel expat-devel libxml2-devel \
+    brotli-devel libmaxminddb-devel udns-devel \
+    libcap-devel libaio-devel
+
+# Configure
+cmake -B build \
+    -DUSE_SYSTEM_LIBS=ON \
+    -DFHS_LAYOUT=ON \
+    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr \
+    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo \
+    -DMOD_PAGESPEED=OFF \
+    -DMOD_SECURITY=OFF \
+    -DMOD_LUA=OFF \
+    -GNinja
+
+# Build
+cmake --build build
+
+# Install (to a staging directory for packaging)
+DESTDIR=/tmp/stage cmake --install build
+```
+
+## Building the RPM
+
+An RPM spec file is provided at `openlitespeed.spec`.  It follows
+OpenMandriva packaging conventions and can be built with:
+
+```sh
+rpmbuild -ba openlitespeed.spec
+```
+
+The spec file:
+
+* Creates an `openlitespeed` system user/group in `%pre`
+* Installs a systemd service (`openlitespeed.service`)
+* Installs a tmpfiles.d snippet for `/var/run/openlitespeed`
+* Marks config files as `%config(noreplace)`
+* Uses `%cmake` / `%cmake_build` / `%cmake_install` macros
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+When both `USE_SYSTEM_LIBS` and `FHS_LAYOUT` are `OFF` (the defaults),
+the build behaves identically to the original upstream — bundled static
+libraries, BoringSSL, static `libstdc++`, and the traditional
+`/usr/local/lsws` monolithic layout.  Existing build scripts and the
+`build.sh` workflow are not affected.
+
+## Configuration File Changes
+
+The `httpd_config.conf.in` template now uses substitution variables for
+paths (`%CONF_DIR%`, `%LOG_DIR%`, `%DOC_ROOT%`, `%FCGI_DIR%`) instead of
+hard-coding relative paths.  The RPM spec's `%install` section performs
+the substitution with `sed`.  Distributions may also generate the config
+at build time via CMake's `configure_file()` if desired.
